UID:roze-filmdagen-2027-submissions@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261111T142941Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261202
SUMMARY:Deadline: Roze Filmdagen 2027: 30th Amsterdam LGBTQ+ Film Festival 
 Submissions
DESCRIPTION:The 30th Roze Filmdagen\, Amsterdam's LGBTQ+ film festival\, is
  accepting short films\, feature films\, documentaries and animations with
  a clear connection to LGBTQ+ themes and sexual\, gender and cultural dive
 rsity\, for its edition of 10-21 March 2027.\n\nOrganisation: Roze Filmdag
 en (Amsterdam LGBTQ+ Film Festival)\nLocation: Amsterdam\, Netherlands (30
 th edition\, 10-21 March 2027). Open to filmmakers worldwide.\nAward: Cash
  prizes (amounts not published): Jury Awards and Audience Awards for best 
 feature\, best documentary and best short\, plus the Free to be Me Award (
 initiated by Hivos). Roze Filmdagen is a nominating festival for the Iris 
 Prize (Cardiff). Listed under the desk's festival exception. Submission fe
 e: none in the 2025 and 2026 editions\; the 2027 FilmFreeway fee could not
  be confirmed.\nDuration: Festival 10-21 March 2027\n\nMore: https://rozef
 ilmdagen.nl/en/news/inzendingen-2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
URL:https://rozefilmdagen.nl/en/news/inzendingen-2027?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Amsterdam\, Netherlands (30th edition\, 10-21 March 2027). Open to
  filmmakers worldwide.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:norma-fonds-projectbijdrage-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261111T142941Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261030
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261031
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stichting NORMA: NORMA Fonds Project Grant (round 4\, 202
 6)
DESCRIPTION:The NORMA Fonds redistributes copyright remuneration collected 
 by Stichting NORMA into cultural\, social and professional projects involv
 ing performing artists\, and is one of the few Dutch schemes with four int
 akes a year and a genuinely short cycle.\n\nOrganisation: Stichting NORMA 
 (collecting society for performing artists)\nLocation: Netherlands-based a
 rts-sector activity. No city or region restriction stated.\nAward: Maximum
  EUR 10\,000 per project. Total project budget may not exceed EUR 150\,000
  and the applicant organisation's annual budget may not exceed EUR 500\,00
 0. At least 25 percent of the project budget must come from audience or bo
 x-office revenue. Performer fees must meet the 2026 wage norms of EUR 139 
 per rehearsal and EUR 340 per performance. No application fee.\nDuration: 
 Single project\, typically a production or concert series. Final report du
 e within six months of completion.\n\nMore: https://www.stichtingnorma.nl/
 norma-fonds/aanvragen/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=re
 ferral
URL:https://www.stichtingnorma.nl/norma-fonds/aanvragen/?utm_source=artific
 ialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands-based arts-sector activity. No city or region restrict
 ion stated.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:go-short-nijmegen-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261111T142941Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261215
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261216
SUMMARY:Deadline: Go Short 2027: International Short Film Festival Nijmegen
  Submissions
DESCRIPTION:Go Short\, the international short film festival in Nijmegen\, 
 is open for entries for its 19th edition (6 to 11 April 2027). A small\, a
 pproachable Dutch festival that programmes fiction\, documentary\, animati
 on and experimental shorts.\n\nOrganisation: Go Short\, International Shor
 t Film Festival Nijmegen\nLocation: Nijmegen\, Netherlands. European Compe
 tition open to films made in Europe\; dedicated Dutch Competition\; New Ar
 rivals Competition for European film school projects.\nAward: Small submis
 sion fees per tier: EUR 12.50 (early bird\, 15 September 2026)\, EUR 15 (r
 egular\, 15 November) or EUR 20 (late\, 15 December) for films\; EUR 8/10/
 12 for video games\, VR/XR\, performances and installations\; EUR 7.50 fla
 t for music videos. Awards include the Go Short Award for Best European Sh
 ort\, Best Dutch Short\, the New Arrivals Award and an Audience Award (amo
 unts not published in the call).\nDuration: Festival 6 to 11 April 2027\n\
 nMore: https://www.goshort.nl/en/news-overview/call-for-entry-go-short-202
 7?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.goshort.nl/en/news-overview/call-for-entry-go-short-2027?ut
 m_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Nijmegen\, Netherlands. European Competition open to films made in
  Europe\; dedicated Dutch Competition\; New Arrivals Competition for Europ
 ean film school projects.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stichting-stokroos-seed-grant-autumn-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261111T142941Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261031
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stichting Stokroos: Seed Grant\, Autumn 2026 round
DESCRIPTION:The Stokroos Seed Grant supports early-practice visual artists\
 , designers and craft practitioners in the Netherlands with an unrestricte
 d budget for a self-defined plan: EUR 5\,000 for individuals\, EUR 7\,500 
 for duos\, EUR 10\,000 for collectives. The plan must start at least 10 we
 eks after submission\, last no longer than a year\, and can take place any
 where in the world.\n\nOrganisation: Stichting Stokroos\nLocation: Applica
 nts must live and work in the Kingdom of the Netherlands (including its Ca
 ribbean parts) or Suriname for at least one year\; the funded plan itself 
 can take place anywhere in the world.\nAward: EUR 5\,000 for individuals\,
  EUR 7\,500 for duos\, EUR 10\,000 for collectives\, as an unrestricted co
 ntribution to a self-defined plan. No application fee.\nDuration: Funded p
 lan starts at least 10 weeks after submission and lasts up to one year\n\n
 More: https://stokroos.nl/en/grant-rules/seed-en/?utm_source=artificialnou
 veaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://stokroos.nl/en/grant-rules/seed-en/?utm_source=artificialnouvea
 ugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Applicants must live and work in the Kingdom of the Netherlands (i
 ncluding its Caribbean parts) or Suriname for at least one year\; the fund
 ed plan itself can take place anywhere in the world.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:movies-that-matter-festival-2027-submissions@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20261111T142941Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Deadline: Movies that Matter Festival 2027: Film Submissions
DESCRIPTION:Movies that Matter\, the human rights film festival in The Hagu
 e (19-27 March 2027)\, is open for 2027 submissions. The festival screens 
 poignant fiction films and revealing documentaries that stir debates about
  human rights\, sustainability and the fight against injustice\, and feeds
  several competitions: the Grand Jury Documentary Competition (eight docum
 entaries\, EUR 5\,000\, winner eligible for...\n\nOrganisation: Movies tha
 t Matter\nLocation: The Hague\, Netherlands (festival 19-27 March 2027)\; 
 submissions open worldwide\, attendance not required for submission.\nAwar
 d: Cash prizes: EUR 5\,000 Grand Jury Documentary award (winner also becom
 es eligible for consideration for the Academy Award for Best Documentary F
 eature)\, EUR 5\,000 Grand Jury Fiction award\, and EUR 1\,500 Shorts awar
 d\; further competitions (Activist Lens\, Justice Frame\, Dutch Focus\, Ed
 ucation Award\, Audience Award) publish no amounts. SUBMISSION FEE: EUR 25
  until 30 September 2026\, EUR 35 late fee 1 October to 1 November 2026\; 
 fee waivers only in very exceptional cases.\n\nMore: https://moviesthatmat
 ter.nl/en/festival/industry/film-submissions/?utm_source=artificialnouveau
 grantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://moviesthatmatter.nl/en/festival/industry/film-submissions/?utm_
 source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:The Hague\, Netherlands (festival 19-27 March 2027)\; submissions 
 open worldwide\, attendance not required for submission.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:witte-rook-izolyatsia-digital-explorers-2027@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20261111T142941Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART:20261115T222900Z
DTEND:20261115T225900Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 23:59 CET: Witte Rook x IZOLYATSIA: Digital Explorers (Acr
 oss Borders) Online Residency 2027
DESCRIPTION:Closes 15 Nov 2026 at 23:59 CET.\n\nWitte Rook (Breda) and the 
 Ukrainian platform IZOLYATSIA run Digital Explorers (Across Borders)\, a f
 ully online residency program exploring the artist-in-residence of the fut
 ure through cross-border collaboration. Each of three phases pairs one art
 ist from the Netherlands with one from Ukraine\, working together for abou
 t three months on the common.garden platform.\n\nOrganisation: Witte Rook 
 and IZOLYATSIA\nLocation: Online\, on the common.garden platform. Open to 
 artists living and working in the Netherlands or Ukraine. Organizers based
  in Breda (NL) and Ukraine.\nAward: EUR 1\,800 artist fee (excluding VAT) 
 plus EUR 1\,000 material budget (excluding VAT) per artist. Six artists se
 lected in total (three Dutch-Ukrainian pairs). No application fee.\nDurati
 on: Approximately three months per phase: Phase 1 'Form' (January to March
  2027)\, Phase 2 'Content' (May to July 2027)\, Phase 3 'Analysis' (Septem
 ber to December 2027).\n\nMore: https://witterook.nl/agenda/open-call-digi
 tal-explorers/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://witterook.nl/agenda/open-call-digital-explorers/?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online\, on the common.garden platform. Open to artists living and
  working in the Netherlands or Ukraine. Organizers based in Breda (NL) and
  Ukraine.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jan-van-eyck-residency-2028@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261111T142941Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART:20261201T222900Z
DTEND:20261201T225900Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 23:59 CET: Jan van Eyck Academie Residency 2028 (Maastrich
 t\, 11 months)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 01 Dec 2026 at 23:59 CET.\n\nThe Jan van Eyck Academie's
  general open call for its 2028 residency year: 30 to 32 artists\, curator
 s\, designers\, writers\, architects and other artistic researchers spend 
 11 months (15 January to 15 December 2028) in Maastricht\, across material
 -based and research-driven practices\, with access to the academy's labs a
 nd community.\n\nOrganisation: Jan van Eyck Academie\nLocation: Maastricht
 \, Netherlands. Open worldwide\; participants must settle in Maastricht an
 d register with the municipality (the academy applies for visas where rele
 vant).\nAward: Monthly stipend of EUR 1\,500 (EUR 2\,000 for participants 
 with children\; EUR 1\,500 per duo member or EUR 2\,500 combined for life 
 partners\; collectives up to EUR 4\,500 combined\, max three stipends)\, w
 ith rent including service costs deducted from the stipend. Plus a EUR 2\,
 000 annual working budget and a newly built\, furnished private studio apa
 rtment. Application fee EUR 65 excl. VAT (EUR 78.65 incl. VAT)\, waived fo
 r applicants from and living in OECD DAC-list countries\; enrolment fee fo
 r accepted participants EUR 2\,750 excl. VAT.\nDuration: 11 months\, 15 Ja
 nuary to 15 December 2028\; 30 to 32 positions\; selection outcome mid-May
  2027.\n\nMore: https://www.janvaneyck.nl/calendar/apply-now-jve-residency
 -2028?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.janvaneyck.nl/calendar/apply-now-jve-residency-2028?utm_sou
 rce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Maastricht\, Netherlands. Open worldwide\; participants must settl
 e in Maastricht and register with the municipality (the academy applies fo
 r visas where relevant).
END:VEVENT
